        "reason": "Choose B3LYP for a uniform single-point comparison of all n-hexane conformers: it is a well-established hybrid GGA functional suitable for closed-shell organic molecules and is explicitly documented in the official ORCA 6.1 DFT manual page. Using one functional across all candidates satisfies the request's single-method/single-basis requirement, while the level stays tractable for many conformers. The source is the ORCA 6.1 'Density Functional Theory' manual entry (Result result_5ec8a462abfd4ae390b46b290b4a6e66) whose document hash is 94424fff...",
