          "source": "explicit"
        },
        "reason": "Choose def2-TZVP as the orbital basis for every conformer single point: the official ORCA 6.1 Basis Sets manual states it is a polarized valence triple-zeta Karlsruhe basis covering H-Rn, directly invoked with the def2-TZVP keyword, with def2-ECP for heavier elements. It is appropriate for an organic molecule of this size and keeps one consistent basis across the entire comparison. The source is the ORCA 6.1 'Basis Sets' manual page (Result result_2e707a63cab74c2591aa329198fed903) whose document hash is 48750fa1....",
